<h2>Care for teens and adults</h2>
<p>Family dentistry means caring for the same patients through the stages of adult life — from a teenager's checkups to the preventive care that keeps your smile healthy for decades. Coordinating care under one roof saves you time, money, and the headache of bouncing between offices.</p>
<!-- CONFIRM: minimum patient age (old site said "ages 12+") -->
<p>We welcome new patients ages 12 and up. <!-- CONFIRM: minimum patient age (old site said "ages 12+") --></p>

<h2>What's included</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Comprehensive exams and digital X-rays</li>
  <li>Cleanings (prophylaxis) and periodontal maintenance</li>
  <li>Fluoride treatments and dental sealants</li>
  <li>Tooth-colored fillings</li>
  <li>Guidance on grinding, clenching, and bite concerns</li>
  <li>Mouthguards for sports and night-time grinding</li>
</ul>

<h2>What a typical visit looks like</h2>
<p>Most healthy patients are on a six-month recall — a routine exam, a professional cleaning, and X-rays once a year. Patients with a history of gum disease or more complex needs may be on a three- or four-month interval. We always tell you why, never just "because."</p>

<h2>New to the practice?</h2>
<p>Visit our <a href="/new-patients/">new patients page</a> to learn what to expect and download any paperwork ahead of your first visit. We try to make first appointments as smooth as possible.</p>
